<headroom-library version="1" id="hg-desert-fuzz-lead" category="High Gain" order="140" instrument="guitar" style="Stoner">
  <description>Stoner rock solo tone: a hot silicon fuzz with an octave-up shadow, into a British valve head and a 4x12, with a warm analog-style echo. Fat, singing and a little unhinged; use the neck pickup, dig into bends and ride the Octave macro for psychedelic peaks.</description>
  <tags><tag>High Gain</tag><tag>Stoner</tag><tag>Desert Rock</tag><tag>Lead</tag><tag>Fuzz</tag><tag>Octave</tag><tag>Delay</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://mixdownmag.com.au/features/a-history-of-josh-hommes-unique-arsenal-of-gear/" title="Mixdown: A history of Josh Homme's gear"/>
    <source url="https://www.premierguitar.com/gear/fu-manchu-fu-zzalicious" title="Premier Guitar: Fu Manchu, Fu-zzalicious"/>
    <source url="https://www.vintageguitar.com/2854/monster-magnet/" title="Vintage Guitar: Monster Magnet"/>
    <source url="https://thesleepingshaman.com/interviews/search-tone-isaiah-mitchell/" title="The Sleeping Shaman: In search of tone, Isaiah Mitchell"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
